course: dictionary
lesson: 14831
title: Two words in one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are joined together from two smaller words. Racecourse is made from race and course. A race is a contest to see who is fastest, and a course is a track or route. Put them together and you get the track where races are held.
explain: «We watched the horses thunder round the racecourse.» The clues are horses, thunder and round. Horses run in races, so a racecourse must be a place where horses race round a track. Always ask: what word would fit here?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in: «We watched the horses thunder round the track.» The sentence still makes sense, so the meaning is right. A racecourse is a track or ground for races, especially horse races.
fact: Racecourse is a noun. Its plural is racecourses.
fact: A racecourse is a track or ground where races are held, especially horse races.
fact: Racecourses have stands, which are seats where people sit to watch the racing.
fact: «Aintree racecourse» is near Liverpool, and it is where the Grand National is run.
fact: Racecourse can also mean any course for racing, such as for cars or runners.
exercise: «We spent a sunny day at the racecourse watching the horses.» Where did they spend the day? | At a swimming pool | On a farm | In a library | *At a racecourse
exercise: What is a racecourse? | A kind of horse | A shop that sells sports clothes | A road for buses | *A track or ground where races are held
exercise: A racecourse is one lap of 400 metres. How far do you run after 3 laps? | 800 metres | 400 metres | *1200 metres | 300 metres
test: Which word is made from two smaller words, race and course? | *racecourse | stadium | racer | horseshoe
test: «The stands at the racecourse were full of cheering fans.» What are the stands? | Horses that run very fast | *Seats where people sit to watch | Bets placed on a race | Gates to the car park
exam: Mia's dad took her to the racecourse to watch the big race. What is a racecourse? | *A track or ground where races are held | A school for learning to ride | A kind of car engine | A shop for race tickets only
